      "children": [
       { "id": "mp-b1p1", "type": "text-block", "settings": { "content": "<p>Marisol runs six small hotels along one stretch of Atlantic coast. They'd grown by acquisition, which meant six logos, six tones of voice and a website that felt like a committee. The brief was deceptively simple: make it one place.</p>", "text_color": "#3a3a3c", "font_size": "19", "line_height": "1.7", "text_align": "left", "max_width": "0" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [] },
       { "id": "mp-b1h3", "type": "headline", "settings": { "heading": "One mark, all weather", "tag": "h3", "heading_font": "heading", "heading_size": "md", "heading_font_size": "26", "heading_color": "#18181a", "heading_weight": "500", "alignment": "left", "decoration": "none" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [] },
       { "id": "mp-b1p2", "type": "text-block", "settings": { "content": "<p>We built the identity around a single horizon line that bends into an \"M\" — a mark that works cast in brass on a door, embroidered on a robe, or animated on a phone. Everything else got out of its way: one typeface, two inks, a lot of paper-coloured space.</p>", "text_color": "#3a3a3c", "font_size": "19", "line_height": "1.7", "text_align": "left", "max_width": "0" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [] }
      ]
     },
     { "id": "mp-co-b1sp2", "type": "column", "settings": { "width": "1-6" }, "style": {}, "advanced": {}, "children": [] }
    ]
   }
  ]
